<mxfile host="65bd71144e">
    <diagram name="FHIR - In general" id="0XPE44v7F9B-mdZ6jX2R">
        <mxGraphModel dx="4660" dy="2665" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
            <root>
                <mxCell id="0"/>
                <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
                <mxCell id="uTYafOiBrDzle6cw7HiI-3" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;HAPI Application FHIR implementation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;→&amp;nbsp;https://hapi.fhir.org/baseR4/Patient&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;X12 270 equivalent → https://hapi.fhir.org/baseR4/CoverageEligibilityRequest/138341222&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 22px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 22px;&quot;&gt;Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (ABDM)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: rgb(63, 63, 63); font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;https://www.nrces.in/ndhm/fhir/r4/index.html - :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;SMART (Substitutable Medical Applications and Reusable Technologies)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&quot;Design and build a serverless, FHIR-compliant analytics pipeline on AWS that ingests streaming patient data via Python, secures it using SMART on FHIR principles, and optimizes it for large-scale queries using AWS HealthLake and Redshift.&quot;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;self-link-parent&quot; style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-family: &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1em; font-size: 19.6px; margin: 0px 0px 0.4em; font-weight: 500; overflow: hidden; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-rendering: optimizelegibility; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;The Standards Development Process :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.4em; font-family: verdana; margin: 0px 0px 10px; padding-bottom: 5px; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;HL7 has five descriptive terms that describe the level of stability and implementation readiness associated with different aspects of the specification. They are as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table style=&quot;margin-bottom: 10px; border-collapse: collapse; border-spacing: 0px; max-width: 100%; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;tbody style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.4em; font-family: verdana; padding: 3px; vertical-align: top;&quot;&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Standard Level&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.4em; font-family: verdana; padding: 3px; vertical-align: top;&quot;&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; text-align: left; background-color: rgb(239, 239, 239); border: 1px solid grey; padding-left: 3px; padding-right: 3px;&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/th&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.4em; padding: 3px; vertical-align: top;&quot;&gt;This portion of the specification is not considered to be complete enough or sufficiently reviewed to be safe for implementation. It may have known issues or still be in the &quot;in development&quot; stage. It is included in the publication as a place-holder, to solicit feedback from the implementation community and/or to give implementers some insight as to functionality likely to be included in future versions of the specification. Content at this level should only be implemented by the brave or desperate and is very much &quot;use at your own risk&quot;. The content that is &lt;i style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;Draft&lt;/i&gt; that will usually be elevated to &lt;i style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;Trial Use&lt;/i&gt; once review and correction is complete after it has been subjected to ballot&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.4em; font-family: verdana; padding: 3px; vertical-align: top;&quot;&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; text-align: left; background-color: rgb(255, 245, 230); border: 1px solid grey; padding-left: 3px; padding-right: 3px;&quot;&gt;Trial Use&lt;/th&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.4em; padding: 3px; vertical-align: top;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.4em; margin: 0px 0px 10px; padding-bottom: 5px;&quot;&gt;This content has been well reviewed and is considered by the authors to be ready for use in production systems. It has been subjected to ballot and approved as an official standard. However, it has not yet seen widespread use in production across the full spectrum of environments it is intended to be used in. In some cases, there may be documented known issues that require implementation experience to determine appropriate resolutions for.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.4em; margin: 0px 0px 10px; padding-bottom: 5px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;Future versions of FHIR may make significant changes to &lt;i style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;Trial Use&lt;/i&gt; content that are not compatible with previously published content.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.4em; font-family: verdana; padding: 3px; vertical-align: top;&quot;&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; text-align: left; background-color: rgb(230, 255, 230); border: 1px solid grey; padding-left: 3px; padding-right: 3px;&quot;&gt;Normative&lt;/th&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.4em; padding: 3px; vertical-align: top;&quot;&gt;This content has been subject to review and production implementation in a wide variety of environments. The content is considered to be stable and has been &#39;locked&#39;, subjecting it to FHIR Inter-version Compatibility Rules. While changes are possible, they are expected to be infrequent and are tightly constrained.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.4em; font-family: verdana; padding: 3px; vertical-align: top;&quot;&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; text-align: left; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 230); border: 1px solid grey; padding-left: 3px; padding-right: 3px;&quot;&gt;Informative&lt;/th&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.4em; padding: 3px; vertical-align: top;&quot;&gt;This portion of the specification is provided for implementer assistance and does not make rules that implementers are required to follow. Typical examples of this content in the FHIR specification are tables of contents, registries, examples, and implementer advice&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.4em; font-family: verdana; padding: 3px; vertical-align: top;&quot;&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; text-align: left; background-color: rgb(255, 204, 204); border: 1px solid grey; padding-left: 3px; padding-right: 3px;&quot;&gt;Deprecated&lt;/th&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.4em; padding: 3px; vertical-align: top;&quot;&gt;This portion of the specification is outdated and may be withdrawn in a future version. Implementers who already support it should continue to do so for backward compatibility. Implementers should avoid adding new uses of this portion of the specification. The specification should include guidance on what implementers should use instead of the deprecated portion&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="1920" width="780" x="30" y="720" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="uTYafOiBrDzle6cw7HiI-4" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="450" width="472.86" x="30" y="20" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="z1BbL5M4AdqJs5WAxIZh-3" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="232" width="462.46" x="30" y="470" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
    <diagram id="xvSTsNDBU-s25AyYXftS" name="FHIR - Profiles">
        <mxGraphModel dx="8100" dy="4442" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
            <root>
                <mxCell id="qkyLPPaMuicFOam1TiuT-0"/>
                <mxCell id="qkyLPPaMuicFOam1TiuT-1" parent="qkyLPPaMuicFOam1TiuT-0"/>
                <mxCell id="6DEfMQowo5a_tk0az3u5-0" parent="qkyLPPaMuicFOam1TiuT-1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;FHIR Profiles&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://hapi.fhir.org/baseR4/swagger-ui/?page=All&lt;div class=&quot;markdown-body&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(230, 237, 243); font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe WPC&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, system-ui, Ubuntu, &amp;quot;Droid Sans&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h1 class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; id=&quot;implementing-fhir-profiles-in-intersystems-iris&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.25; padding-bottom: 0.3em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-top-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-right-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-left-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18);&quot;&gt;Implementing FHIR Profiles in InterSystems IRIS&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;This is a concise self-learning note based on the article &quot;Implementing FHIR Profiles in IRIS&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; id=&quot;1-what-is-a-fhir-profile&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.25; padding-bottom: 0.3em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-top-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-right-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-left-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18);&quot;&gt;1) What is a FHIR profile?&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;A FHIR profile is a constrained version of a base resource such as &lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;Patient&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;Observation&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;Medication&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0.7em;&quot;&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Base FHIR is generic and broad.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A profile adds rules for a specific use case, hospital, region, or workflow.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The goal is not to replace FHIR, but to make the data more precise and interoperable.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;Examples of profile rules:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0.7em;&quot;&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;required fields&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;allowed cardinality&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;fixed values or patterns&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;allowed coded values (&lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;ValueSet&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;required extensions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;slicing for repeating elements&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; id=&quot;2-why-profiles-matter&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.25; padding-bottom: 0.3em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-top-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-right-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-left-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18);&quot;&gt;2) Why profiles matter&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;A valid FHIR resource must be structurally correct. A profile adds clinical and implementation-specific validation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;For example:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0.7em;&quot;&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;Patient.gender&lt;/code&gt; may be allowed in base FHIR but restricted locally to only &lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;male&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;female&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;Patient.identifier&lt;/code&gt; may require a national ID or MRN&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;Observation.code&lt;/code&gt; may be limited to approved local codes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;This is how organizations enforce consistency without changing the base standard.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; id=&quot;3-core-fhir-artifacts&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.25; padding-bottom: 0.3em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-top-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-right-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-left-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18);&quot;&gt;3) Core FHIR artifacts&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; id=&quot;structuredefinition&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.25; font-size: 1.25em;&quot;&gt;StructureDefinition&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;The profile itself. It defines the rules.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;Key fields:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0.7em;&quot;&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;url&lt;/code&gt;: canonical identifier&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;baseDefinition&lt;/code&gt;: base resource or parent profile&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;derivation&lt;/code&gt;: usually &lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;constraint&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;snapshot&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(125, 133, 144); background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.357em;&quot;&gt;differential&lt;/code&gt;: flattened or delta rules&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; id=&quot;valueset&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.25; font-size: 1.25em;&quot;&gt;ValueSet&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;Defines allowed values for a coded element.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; id=&quot;codesystem&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.25; font-size: 1.25em;&quot;&gt;CodeSystem&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;Defines all possible codes and meanings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; id=&quot;extension&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.25; font-size: 1.25em;&quot;&gt;Extension&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;Adds extra fields without altering the base resource.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; id=&quot;4-common-profile-patterns&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.25; padding-bottom: 0.3em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-top-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-right-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18); border-left-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18);&quot;&gt;4) Common profile patterns&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;code-line&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; id=&quot;required-fields&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.25; font-size: 1.25em;&quot;&gt;Required fields&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;pre style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; position: relative; background-color: rgba(110, 118, 129, 0.4); border: 2.4px rgb(230, 237, 243); padding: 16px; border-radius: 3px; overflow: auto; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;code-line language-json&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;font-family: Consolas, &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;, monospace; color: rgb(230, 237, 243); background-image: none; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; font-size: 1